enable scaleLint;

use "@std"
use "@audio"

Note: LINT-01/LINT-02/LINT-03 integration smoke (Phase 24 Plan 24-05)
Note:
Note: flow-interpreter does NOT run an LSP frontend, so this smoke verifies:
Note:   1. `enable scaleLint;` is accepted by PragmaRegistry.KnownPragmas (Plan 24-01)
Note:   2. The file parses + renders without error end-to-end
Note:   3. The pragma is closed-set integration-checked
Note:
Note: Per-diagnostic assertions (LINT-01 F#4 flagged, LINT-02 pragma-absent silent,
Note: LINT-03 inner key Gmajor wins) live in flow-lang.Tests/Unit/Phase24/
Note: ScaleLintAnalyzerFacts.cs:
Note:   - NonDiatonic_FsharpInCmajor_FlagsOneDiagnostic   (LINT-01)
Note:   - PragmaAbsent_NeverFlags_LINT02                  (LINT-02)
Note:   - NestedKeys_InnermostWins_NoFlag                 (LINT-03 — inner Gmajor wins)

Note: LINT-01 canary — F#4 inside `key Cmajor { ... }` would surface a squiggle
Note: in an LSP-aware editor; flow-interpreter just renders silently.
tempo 120 {
    key Cmajor {
        section lint_canary {
            | C4q D4q E4q F#4q G4q |
        }
    }
}

Note: LINT-03 invariant — innermost key wins. F#4 is non-diatonic in Cmajor
Note: but IS diatonic in Gmajor; the squiggle would NOT appear in an LSP editor.
Note: Replaced REQUIREMENTS.md's Aminor example per CONTEXT specifics line 171.
tempo 120 {
    key Cmajor {
        key Gmajor {
            section nested_inner_wins {
                | F#4q |
            }
        }
    }
}

Song song = [lint_canary nested_inner_wins]
Buffer audio = (renderSong song "piano")
(writeWav "/tmp/flow_test_scale_lint.wav" audio)

(print "test_scale_lint: PASSED")
